-- SCOPE (binding, ledger L8av): the SPLIT per-call premises of the QUAD class (`Tools/ShippingQuadCalls.lean`), exercised on TWO instances: `topshare` (callees `wrap`, `wrap3`, leaf `acc`)
-- and `topshare2` (callees `wrapQ`, `wrapP`, leaf `leaf16`; generated by `Tests/Compiler/SharedLeafGenTest.lean` with `sparkle.sharedLeafCandidate`).  For each instance the OLD per-callee `hcalls`
-- (`ts0_C_hcalls` / `ts1_C_hcalls` / `epD2M{0,1}_C_hcalls`, one text-supplied hypothesis per callee) is RE-DERIVED per call by `leafCallee_hcalls` from: the leaf's generated `seq_child_runN`
-- (`LeafSeqRunN`) and the per-call output equation `CallFactF` of the callee (the old chain's `gfHb*` / `gfHv*` facts + `decoded_eq`, extracted by `oldGroupFact%`); the RANGE `R` of the arguments
-- (the old `gfR*`) is DERIVED (`call_inRange`).  Likewise the parent's `QuadGroupFacts` is `quadGroupFacts_of_RF (quad_inRange …) hFP`, with only `hFP` (`CallFactF`) text-supplied.
-- The statement of each re-derived theorem is INFERRED from the generic lemma and compared by `isDefEq` with the OLD statement (old theorems untouched), with a mismatch audit; then
-- `*_returned4` / `*_wired4` apply the generic `quad_returned` / `quad_wired` with `composed` := `quad_composed_split`, and a closure audit checks the old `hcalls` blocks are NOT in the closure.
-- TEXT-SUPPLIED premises that remain (named, NOT derived): `GenFacts` of the parent / callees (the generated `machine_*` facts), `LeafSeqRunN` (`leaf.seq_child_runN`), `CallFactF` of every callee and of the
-- parent (the output equation at the call-output position), `hext` / `hextB` of the callees (`seq_child_runN_ofR1`), the `Inhabited` instances, and the decided data facts.
-- TWO instances do NOT make the class complete.  `RealChildA` / `ServedRealA` / `JQC` / `MachineRunNCA` are histories of past synthesis results, not freshness or semantic correctness.
-- No `sorry`, no `axiom`, no `native_decide`.
